---

Kanji stroke geometry: CC BY-SA 3.0
------------------------------------

The `type`, `start`, `end`, and `svgPath` fields of each entry in the
`strokes` array inside public/js/data.js are stroke geometry -- rescaled
and reclassified, not independently drawn -- derived from KanjiVG
(https://github.com/KanjiVG/kanjivg), Copyright (C) 2009-2011 Ulrich Apel,
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported
license (CC BY-SA 3.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/).

CC BY-SA 3.0's ShareAlike clause (Section 4(b)) requires that an adaptation
of the licensed material itself be distributed under CC BY-SA 3.0 (or a
later version of this license, or another CC-compatible license). In
compliance with that requirement -- not merely as a notice to downstream
users -- this project licenses that stroke geometry data as follows:

  The `type`/`start`/`end`/`svgPath` stroke geometry fields in
  public/js/data.js are themselves licensed under CC BY-SA 3.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/), with attribution to
  KanjiVG (https://github.com/KanjiVG/kanjivg) and Ulrich Apel.

If you extract and reuse that geometry data, alone or combined with new
work, your result must likewise credit KanjiVG and be released under
CC BY-SA 3.0 or a CC-compatible license. This requirement applies only to
that geometry data -- the rest of this repository remains available under
the MIT license above.

---

Hiragana/katakana stroke geometry: LGPL-3.0-or-later
------------------------------------------------------

The same split applies to the kana entries in public/js/data.js (the
hiragana/katakana categories): the `type`, `start`, `end`, and `svgPath`
fields of each `strokes` entry are geometry -- rescaled and reclassified,
not independently drawn -- derived from animCJK's Japanese kana SVGs
(https://github.com/parsimonhi/animCJK, `svgsJaKana/`). Per that project's
own licensing notice, those kana SVG files (unlike its kanji/hanzi ones,
which are derived from Arphic fonts under different terms) are licensed
under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 or later
(LGPL-3.0-or-later, full text in third_party_licenses/LGPL-3.0.txt and
https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.html, which in turn incorporates
GPL-3.0 by reference -- see https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html).

The LGPL is written for software libraries, but its copyleft (modifying
and redistributing "the Library" requires the modified version to remain
under the same license) applies just as much to this rescaled/reclassified
geometry data as it would to modified library source. In compliance with
that requirement:

  The `type`/`start`/`end`/`svgPath` stroke geometry fields for the
  hiragana/katakana entries in public/js/data.js are themselves licensed
  under LGPL-3.0-or-later, with attribution to the animCJK project.

If you extract and reuse that kana geometry data, alone or combined with
new work, your result must likewise credit animCJK and be released under
LGPL-3.0-or-later. This requirement applies only to that geometry data --
the rest of this repository remains available under the MIT license
above (and the kanji stroke geometry stays CC BY-SA 3.0, as described
above).
